minium, with its glass wall onto the Abby Aldrich Rockefeller Sculpture Garden (marble paving, two pools, trees) and the Education Building across the garden; Diller Scofidio + Renfro's 2019 Geffen Wing; Jean Nouvel's tapering 53W53 (320 m) at the west end. The two towers are cut off at 72 m so the museum can be read at this scale (Museum Tower goes on to about 160 m, 53W53 to 320 m); only their lower floors, which hold galleries, are shown. Positions and heights from the ground file (Museum Tower, 53W53, the streets) and published descriptions (Dezeen, Architizer, e-architect, NYRB). Guessed: the exact widths along 53rd Street, the diagrid (only hinted by horizontal ribs), the canopy's round openings (left out), the neighbours. No photographs were available."}